# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# Patterns, not literal filenames. This previously listed exactly
# "config.yaml" and "gs4creds.json", so a copy or rename (config_2026.yaml,
# creds.json) would have been committed silently. Note that "*.env" does NOT
# match a bare ".env" -- hence ".env*" below.
config*.yaml
config*.yml
!config.example.yaml
*creds*.json
*credential*.json
service-account*.json
.env*
*.env
*.pem
*.key

# --- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- R -------------------------------------------------------------------
.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# --- OS ------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Data/G2/ is deliberately NOT ignored, and it is the one data directory in this
# repo that must not be. Everything else under Data/ is either regenerable from a
# pull or rebuildable from the pipeline; the G2 archive is neither. It is the
# pre-season 2026 board blended with and without USG_, and once week 1 is played
# the inputs have moved and it cannot be reconstructed -- FantasyPros serves no
# season parameter, so a past board is gone the moment it stops being current.
# Plan 18 records G2 as unmeasurable on history for exactly that reason. This
# archive is the only thing that makes it measurable going forward.

# --- Regenerable local data ------------------------------------------------
# Equivalence snapshots: large, and rebuilt from the pipeline on demand.
Data/Equivalence/
# The local data store the app reads. Rebuilt by `python -m Scripts.refresh`,
# and a lineups.parquet is ~235 x 469 per league-season.
Data/Store/
# nflverse usage pulls, rebuilt by `Rscript R/GetUsage.R` -- ~3.5 MB a season and
# regenerable in seconds. Listed by filename rather than as Data/NFL/*/ because
# Data/NFL/2025/NFL_Stats.csv is committed. Data/NFL/player_ids.parquet is
# committed too, and is not season-scoped, so it is unaffected either way.
Data/NFL/*/opportunity.parquet
Data/NFL/*/player_weeks.parquet
Data/NFL/*/usage_meta.json
# Availability and role pulls, rebuilt by `Rscript R/GetContext.R`. Same argument.
# depth_charts is the big one: ~35k rows a season through 2024 and 549k for 2025,
# where upstream switched the feed to a timestamped snapshot log.
Data/NFL/*/rosters_weekly.parquet
Data/NFL/*/injuries.parquet
Data/NFL/*/snap_counts.parquet
Data/NFL/*/depth_charts.parquet
Data/NFL/*/context_meta.json
# Role-resolving pulls, rebuilt by `Rscript R/GetAdvanced.R`. Same argument again,
# except that these are the expensive ones: routes and red_zone both need full
# play-by-play, so a cold backfill is minutes rather than seconds. Contracts is
# not season-scoped and is small, but it is still a straight nflreadr pull with
# nothing merged into it, so it regenerates identically and is ignored too.
Data/NFL/*/routes.parquet
Data/NFL/*/ngs.parquet
Data/NFL/*/red_zone.parquet
Data/NFL/*/advanced_meta.json
Data/NFL/contracts.parquet
# Coach-per-game and team names, rebuilt by `Rscript R/GetCoaches.R`. The *derived*
# Data/NFL/coaching_staff.parquet is committed -- it merges in Wikipedia data that
# cannot be regenerated identically once an article is edited.
Data/NFL/coaches_by_game.parquet
Data/NFL/team_names.parquet
